@startuml qnx_dispatch_engine_cleanup_activity
title QnxDispatchEngine - owner cleanup

start
if (Entry is ProcessCleanup(owner)?) then (yes)
    :Remove matching-owner endpoints from posix_endpoint_list_\nFor each, call UnselectEndpoint();
    note right
        UnselectEndpoint invalidates a found poll slot,
        unregisters its select/ping events and invokes
        the disconnect callback if present.
    end note
    :TimedCommandQueue::CleanUpOwner(owner)\nlock the queue mutex;
    while (Another matching-owner queue entry?) is (yes)
        :Unlink the matching entry;
        :Unlock the queue mutex;
        :Reset its callback, destroying captures without invocation;
        :Relock the queue mutex;
    endwhile (no)
    :Unlock and return from ProcessCleanup;
    stop
else (CleanUpOwner)
    :Inspect the owner argument;
endif

if (owner is nullptr?) then (yes)
    :Return without touching endpoints or commands;
    stop
else (non-null)
    :Determine IsOnCallbackThread();
endif
if (Caller is on either engine dispatch thread?) then (yes)
    :Invoke the ProcessCleanup(owner) procedure inline;
    :Return to the callback-thread caller;
    stop
else (other thread)
    :Create a stack cleanup entry and NonAllocatingFuture\nusing the client runner mutex and cleanup_ready_condition_;
endif
:RegisterImmediateEntry with TimePoint{} and this owner\nContinuation calls ProcessCleanup(owner), then future.MarkReady();
:WakeUpTimerQueue() to request client-thread dispatch;
:future.Wait()\ncheck readiness under the client runner mutex\nWait on the condition variable while not ready;
note right
    Waiting releases the mutex.
    MarkReady sets readiness and notifies under the same mutex.
    Readiness may already be set before Wait starts.
end note
:Return after the cleanup continuation acknowledges completion;
stop

legend
    No timeout is supplied for cleanup acknowledgement.
    The engine rejects null owners, whereas the queue helper treats
    nullptr as an ordinary matching key.
    This is not a barrier against concurrent or reentrant submissions.
endlegend

@enduml
